# Repository root. The package folder has its own .gitignore for build products.

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Measurement captures. Conclusions drawn from them live in docs/05_results.md;
# the captures themselves are machine-specific and not reproducible elsewhere.
*.mat
*.csv

# Editor and OS clutter
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Earlier versions stay on disk and off GitHub. They are reference copies: 0.3.1
# was never published at all (its notes were folded into 0.4.0), and 0.3.0 is
# essentially the flat layout that is already in this repository's first commit,
# so publishing it as a folder would duplicate history that a tag records
# better. Nothing here affects the release: `make package` copies only from
# PsychMetal-0.4.0/, so the zip is the same either way.
#
# Delete either line to publish that version as a folder.
PsychMetal-0.3.0/
PsychMetal-0.3.1/

# The release script sits here, beside the versioned package folder rather than
# inside it, so it cannot reach the release zip or a user's path. It is also not
# published: it is a maintainer's tool with one user, and it names a GitHub
# account. Delete this line if you would rather it were in the repository.
release-*.sh
